[00:21.69]1. Our happy God is merciful,
[00:27.02]His mercy not just dutiful.
[00:32.36]He takes delight in kindly deeds
[00:37.69]And freely grants our daily needs.
[00:47.08]Repentant ones can be assured
[00:51.08]Their plea for mercy will be heard.
[00:57.08]Remembering that we are dust,
[01:04.08]He’s merciful and kind and just.
[01:37.63]2. When we have sinned and feel distressed,
[01:49.07]When God’s forgiveness we request,
[01:53.07]Our Lord, Christ Jesus, showed the way
[01:57.07]To ask for mercy when we pray:
[02:02.01]“Forgive our debts, we beg of you,
[02:08.35]As we forgive our debtors too.”
[02:14.59]We then can let resentment go,
[02:20.99]And peace of mind and heart we’ll know.
[02:47.32]3. When gifts of mercy we bestow,
[02:52.32]The giving spirit we should show.
[02:58.32]We give without desiring praise,
[03:05.32]Content with joy our gift conveys.
[03:14.16]Then God, who sees all things we do,
[03:18.16]Will be the One repaying you.
[03:24.16]Yes, happy are the merciful,
[03:31.16]In God’s eyes they are beautiful.